  "description": "Fuaran.Compute.GeometricAlgebraOps — geometric transforms as a parametric op algebra over Fuaran.Compute.GeometricAlgebra: a state of named objects, generic in the name, whose comparison and spelling the caller supplies; seven ops — Add an object from its parameters (a point; two points; a point and a direction; a centre, a radius and a normal; a normal and a distance; a centre and a radius), Remove, Rotate about an axis through a point, Translate, Scale about a centre, Reflect in a plane, and Screw, the general rigid motion — each carrying parameters and never a coefficient; a total apply and canApply that refuse by name and leave the state as it was; an inverse for six of the seven; the compaction of a run of rigid transforms of one object into one op; a canonical wire codec that writes every float as its IEEE-754 bit pattern; and a Fuaran.Core.OpStream StreamWitness, so a history of transforms is an append-only, hash-chained, replayable stream. Replay builds every object and every versor through the algebra's published constructors and applies it by their published sandwich, and computes nothing of its own: the same bits on .NET, under Fable and in every host that transcribes it. Fable-clean.",
